kate (Docs): Quick sync — I'm updating the troubleshooting matrix for throttling/429s, timeouts, and context-limit fallbacks. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/842. Need: 1) short SDK snippets for handling 429 + jittered backoff, 2) streaming fallback example, 3) link fixes to runtime behavior section. Can @rahul + @miguel take ownership of code snippets?

rahul (SDK): on it. I updated JS + Py snippets in the PR but left placeholders for streaming fallback. Need to confirm recommended default backoff params. Is 200ms base with 2x expo and jitter ok?

miguel (Eng): 200ms base is fine for our hosted tier; for Dedicated maybe bump to 500ms. Also add explicit guidance: if you see sustained 429s, suggest routing to fallback model via routing policy (see runtime docs). I'll paste a short note.

miguel (Eng): Runtime note:
```
If model A hits capacity-induced 429s, smart routing can failover to model B (smaller quantized variant) within ~100-300ms. This is not an immediate retry loop — prefer exponential backoff + single failover attempt.
```

samir (PM): We should also call out UX expectations: users will see transient 429s during bursts; docs should show metric to watch: token_429_rate and per-route p95 latency. Add link to console metrics.

kate (Docs): Good call. @rahul can you add the jittered backoff snippet and a streaming fallback example that calls the fallback route? Keep both JS and Python. I'll handle the console metrics link and wording. Deadline EOD Thursday for merge.

rahul (SDK): snippet added — placed under examples/429-handling in the PR. JS:
```
async function callWithRetry() {
  let delay = 200;
  for (let i=0;i<5;i++){
    try {
      return await api.generate(...);
    } catch (e) {
      if (e.status === 429) {
        await sleep(delay * (0.8 + Math.random()*0.4));
        delay *= 2;
        continue;
      }
      throw e;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('max retries');
}
```

rahul (SDK): streaming fallback (pseudo):
```
// open stream to primary
// on 429 or stream error -> open stream to fallback model endpoint
// emit a short notice to the client about degraded model fidelity
```

miguel (Eng): added a short log excerpt to the PR showing failover decision (timestamped) — gave permission to quote.

